          "measurementTechnique": {
            "description": "A technique, method or technology used in the source data for the data collection corresponding to the method used for measuring the corresponding variable(s) (for the records in the data collection, described using variableMeasured; for Observation, a StatisticalVariable). For example, if variableMeasured is: molecule concentration, measurementTechnique could be: \"mass spectrometry\" or \"nmr spectroscopy\" or \"colorimetry\" or \"immunofluorescence\". If the variableMeasured is \"depression rating\", the measurementTechnique could be \"Zung Scale\" or \"HAM-D\" or \"Beck Depression Inventory\".",
            "abstract": "Methods or technologies used to generate the resource",
